    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is now implemented in `solution.py`. The 24 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage report. The tests exercise every branch in `solution.py`, so I expect the 90% gate to pass.\n\nIt follows all seven rules in `spec.md`, including normalisation, the unsafe-path checks and skipping directory entries. A bad `dest` raises `ValueError`. Any unsafe member raises `UnsafePathError`, so the function never returns a partial plan. Duplicate names are detected case-insensitively.\n\nI made two choices where the spec was silent. A drive prefix only counts when the first character is an ASCII letter followed by `:`, so `1:x` is treated as an ordinary name. Duplicate detection only compares file members, so a directory entry never clashes with a file of the same name.",
